From: CI Bot <ci@example.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Mar 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: adapt to PyTorch nightly CachingHostAllocator API changes

PyTorch nightly changed the CachingHostAllocator API:
- HostBlockPool::blocks renamed to blocks_
- HostBlockPool removed the unmapped member
- process_events() signature changed to require BlockPool& parameter

The base class CachingHostAllocatorImpl now defines BlockPool as a typedef
to HostBlockPool, which conflicts with the local BlockPool struct defined
in this file. This patch renames the local BlockPool to ExpandableBlockPool
to avoid the name collision.

